  #
  # Each method below is one plan event (`server: true`): call it from the controller or job that
  # makes the event happen. It sends only when the deployment sets TORQUELIFT_JITSU_SERVER_KEY and
  # TORQUELIFT_JITSU_HOST, it sends on a background thread so the response is not held, and it
  # never raises into the caller. It uses only Ruby's standard library.
  #
  # The visitor's anonymous ID rides along when the `torque_lift_aid` cookie is present, which the
  # browser module sets only while the visitor has consented to analytics. Server events are sent
  # without browser consent (they describe what the server did, not what the visitor's browser
  # holds).
